review:
I WANT TO DOWNVOTE THIS GAME SO BAD JUST SO I CAN GET EVEN.
I'M SCARED SH*TLESS  ;-; 

I can't play without pausing every minute. Never has a horror game has me shaking LMAO

[i]Resident Evil 7[/i] is fantastic a game that knows how to mix investigation and survival horror.

[h1]Pros[/h1]
- Interesting story with intriguing characters;
- Cool riddles that connects to the plot;
- Imersive gameplay with a wonderful atmosphere;
- Good soundtracks.

[h1]Cons[/h1]
- None.

From RE series I only played old and remade RE2 - and had a really good fun - so finaly, in 2021, I decided to check what the RE7 hype is all about. And I don't like where RE series went at all..... I returned the game after 2hs of play (but I watched on youtube what to expect in next hours, to confirm I made a right choice):

- First of all the pricing of RE games is a joke for what those games offer. Even the old titles are at full price - only buy them when there is a discount;
- Some graphics look like made for PS2 20 years ago (e.g. shadows). Also, this 2017 game does not work well on highest settings on modern PC... Its probably a result of both simplified console graphics and lazy PC port. First I thought its something wrong with my PC but no - other people had the same problems for years and the producer did nothing about it (still demanding high price...);
- All game is about small, linear locations, couple of canibals/monsters jumping on you out of nowhere and preset situations in which you dont feel like you could do anything about them. Its like watching grade B low budget horrors - all about showing you blood and torture, without caring about the plot. There were hundreds of movies/games like that and this one is no better. Perhaps if you enjoy spending money on such movies, the game is for you.

I wish they stayed with RE2 concept of movie-like action-horror with more logical situations and fast-paced enjoyable story.

As I prepare for Village's release, I have but on thing to say;

" W E L C O M E  T O  T H E  F A M I L Y    ( S   O   N   /   D   A   U   G   H   T   E   R ) "

Nuff said.

I purchased this game during the Autumn Steam Sale;

In my opinion, this game is a must-have and must play. Plays great, looks great. Definitely has its jump scares that almost gave me whiplash and has an overall creepy undertone and unsettling atmosphere. Whenever you think you are getting the hang of things and have an upper hand, this game is going to knock you right back down. The boss battles are great and once you figure out to conquer them and get that sweet victory, it is so fulfilling. At first I thought it would just be kind of a linear haunted house style story, but the writers for this one did a hell of a job at keeping me invested and wanting more and more.

To hold off on rambling, buy this game. If you get lucky like I did and can get it on sale for $10, do it. No regrets. Capcom did a hell of a job.

RE7:
+ good horror;
+ nice story line;
+ interesting gameplay moments;
+ amazing DLC for (achievers or killers);
+ cool level design;
+ scary moments in game get you feel a live. 
- I miss Leon;
- no Leon; 
- Leon was here? ;
Recommended this game for people who like RE series :3

Wow, CAPCOM actually did it, they revived the series.

This game truly goes back to it's survival horror roots, without sacrificing it's trademark action and gruesomeness.

The funny thing is, at first, due to the First Person perspective, you think that it's going to be an entirely different game. However, once you play it for a bit, it all comes together, you see that this is a true RE game! 

- safe rooms with save stations; 
- herbs!
- item management and ammo conservation;
- locked rooms, key hunting and backtracking;
- maps and puzzles and stuff;
- strange characters and gruesome bosses;
- HEEEEEEEERBS!!!!!!!!!!!!!

This game is both a survival horror masterpiece and a love-letter to all RE fans.

Highly recommend.

P.S. Check out the DLC, it's also pretty good!

game time is too short;
new protagonist not related to the main storyline;
no signs of bioharzard, more like silent hill;
graphics not as good as expected;

conculsion: wait for the discount, DLCs and patches before you place the order..

I really like this game. This IS Resident Evil I always wanted to play.
1) It has cool puzzles, like classic REs have;
2) It has dynamic boss battles like shooter-esque REs have;
3) It has great horror atmosphere and tension without using excessive number of screamers.

I totally disagree with people, who compare this to Outlast or to the teaser of cancelled Silent Hills project. These games are absolutely different and have nothing to do with each other.
